        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(e2e): bound Docker stats sample lines",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes (Codex)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Docker E2E resource-ceiling checks could keep accumulating an oversized stats JSONL sample line before rejecting it, letting a malformed or stalled stats writer consume unnecessary memory.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe stats scanner now counts streamed sample-line bytes and rejects any single sample line over 1 MiB before JSON parsing. Normal newline-delimited Docker stats samples still stream through the same resource ceiling checks, including LF, CRLF, and standalone CR delimiters.\n\n## User Impact\n\nE2E resource checks fail fast on oversized Docker stats samples while continuing to accept valid bounded samples.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: 2943390520d66ffd61b5e26b71a5d365f92c3b8a\n\n- Exact-head runtime proof: `node --input-type=module -` created valid, oversized, and CRLF Docker stats samples, then exercised `scripts/e2e/lib/docker-stats/assert-resource-ceiling.mjs` on current head `2943390520d66ffd61b5e26b71a5d365f92c3b8a`.\n\n```text\nhead=2943390520d66ffd61b5e26b71a5d365f92c3b8a\nvalid status=0 stdout=\"proof-valid resource peak: memory=128.0MiB cpu=25.0% samples=1\"\noversized status=1 stderr=\"Error: docker stats sample for proof-oversized exceeded 1048576 bytes\"\ncrlf bytes=1048576 status=0 stdout=\"proof-crlf resource peak: memory=128.0MiB cpu=25.0% samples=1\"\n```\n\n- Exact-head GitHub checks after rebase passed on `2943390520d66ffd61b5e26b71a5d365f92c3b8a`: Real behavior proof, OpenGrep - PR Diff, check-test-types, check-lint, check-prod-types, check-dependencies, build-artifacts, and openclaw/ci-gate.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check -- scripts/e2e/lib/docker-stats/assert-resource-ceiling.mjs test/scripts/docker-stats-resource-ceiling.test.ts` passed.",
        "branch": "qingminglong/docker-stats-line-cap",
